{"key":"moonbitlang/async/js_async.JsError","pkg":"moonbitlang/async/js_async","name":"JsError","parent":"moonbitlang/async/js_async","kind":"type","sig_":"type JsError","doc":"A JavaScript exception wrapped in MoonBit error","attrs":[]}
{"key":"moonbitlang/async/io.Data.text:Method","pkg":"moonbitlang/async/io","name":"text","parent":"moonbitlang/async/io.Data","kind":"method","sig_":"pub fn &Data::text(Self) -> String raise","doc":"Decode data as a UTF8 encoded string.\n\n Calling this method will cause string decoding,\n so user should avoid calling `.text()` more than once.","attrs":[]}
{"key":"moonbitlang/async.Timer.cancel:Method","pkg":"moonbitlang/async","name":"cancel","parent":"moonbitlang/async.Timer","kind":"method","sig_":"pub fn Timer::cancel(Self, err? : Error) -> Unit","doc":"Manually cancel a timer.\n All waiters on the timer will fail immediately with `err`\n (`TimerCancelled` by default).\n All subsequent waiters will also fail with `err` immediately.","attrs":[]}
{"key":"moonbitlang/async.TaskGroup.spawn_bg:Method","pkg":"moonbitlang/async","name":"spawn_bg","parent":"moonbitlang/async.TaskGroup","kind":"method","sig_":"pub fn[X] TaskGroup::spawn_bg(Self[X], async () -> Unit, no_wait? : Bool, allow_failure? : Bool) -> Unit","doc":"Spawn a child task in a task group, and run it asynchronously in the background.\n\n Unless `no_wait` (`false` by default) is `true`,\n the task group will wait for this task to complete before normal exit.\n No matter what the value of `no_wait` is,\n `with_task_group` will only return after all child tasks terminate.\n The task will be cancelled automatically if it is still running\n when the task group wishes to terminate,\n\n Unless `allow_failure` (`false` by default) is `true`,\n the whole task group will also fail if the spawned task fails, \n other tasks in the group will be cancelled in this case.\n\n Cancelled task (either cancelled by the group or manually cancelled via `Task::cancel`)\n are not consider failing, although they raise a cancellation error.\n However, if the task raise some other error during cancellation handling,\n it will be considered failing.\n\n If the task group is already cancelled, but `with_task_group` is still running\n (i.e. there are still other running child task in the group),\n `spawn_bg` will still succeed, but the child task will be cancelled immediately.\n In this case, the child task still get a chance to start execution\n (which means you can rely on `defer` at the start of child task being triggered),\n but will be in cancelled state from the very beginning\n (e.g. all async IO operation will be cancelled immediately before starting).\n\n Calling `spawn_bg` after `with_task_group` completed or inside `group.add_defer` \n is not allowed, and will abort the program immediately.\n\n It is undefined whether the child task will start running immediately\n before `spawn_bg` returns.","attrs":[]}
{"key":"moonbitlang/async/internal/io_buffer.Buffer","pkg":"moonbitlang/async/internal/io_buffer","name":"Buffer","parent":"moonbitlang/async/internal/io_buffer","kind":"type","sig_":"struct Buffer","doc":null,"attrs":[]}
{"key":"moonbitlang/core/debug.Debug_for_moonbitlang/async/io.PipeClosed","pkg":"moonbitlang/async/io","name":"moonbitlang/core/debug.Debug_for_moonbitlang/async/io.PipeClosed","parent":null,"kind":["impl","moonbitlang/core/debug.Debug","moonbitlang/async/io.PipeClosed"],"sig_":"pub impl @debug.Debug for PipeClosed","doc":null,"attrs":[]}
{"key":"moonbitlang/core/builtin.ToJson_for_moonbitlang/async/io.ReaderClosed","pkg":"moonbitlang/async/io","name":"moonbitlang/core/builtin.ToJson_for_moonbitlang/async/io.ReaderClosed","parent":null,"kind":["impl","moonbitlang/core/builtin.ToJson","moonbitlang/async/io.ReaderClosed"],"sig_":"pub impl ToJson for ReaderClosed","doc":null,"attrs":[]}
{"key":"moonbitlang/async.TaskGroup.spawn_loop:Method","pkg":"moonbitlang/async","name":"spawn_loop","parent":"moonbitlang/async.TaskGroup","kind":"method","sig_":"pub fn[X] TaskGroup::spawn_loop(Self[X], async () -> Unit, no_wait? : Bool, allow_failure? : Bool, retry? : RetryMethod, max_retry? : Int, fatal_error? : (Error) -> Bool) -> Unit","doc":"Similar to `spawn_bg`, but the spawn a loop,\n i.e. the spawned task will be restarted after it terminates.\n The spawned task can terminate the loop by raising\n the special error `BreakFromSpawnLoop`,\n the loop will terminate normally instead of failing in this case.\n\n If `retry_method` is set, within each loop,\n the spawned task will be automatically restarted on failure.\n The restart strategy is determined by the value of `retry_method`.\n `max_retry` and `fatal_error` will be passed as-is to `retry`.\n See `retry` and `RetryMethod` for more details.\n\n The meaning of `no_wait` and `allow_failure` is the same as `spawn_bg`.","attrs":[]}
{"key":"moonbitlang/async/websocket.unimplemented","pkg":"moonbitlang/async/websocket","name":"unimplemented","parent":"moonbitlang/async/websocket","kind":"let","sig_":"pub let unimplemented : Unit","doc":"This package currently does not support JavaScript backend","attrs":[]}
{"key":"moonbitlang/async/js_async.AbortController.new:Method","pkg":"moonbitlang/async/js_async","name":"new","parent":"moonbitlang/async/js_async.AbortController","kind":"method","sig_":"pub fn AbortController::new() -> Self","doc":"Create a new abort controller","attrs":[]}
