{"key":"moonbitlang/async/io.PipeRead.drop:Method","pkg":"moonbitlang/async/io","name":"drop","parent":"moonbitlang/async/io.PipeRead","kind":"method","sig_":"pub async fn PipeRead::drop(Self, Int) -> Int","doc":"`reader.drop(len)` drops `len` number of bytes from the reader.\n The number of bytes actually dropped is returned.\n `drop` will wait until enough number of bytes is available,\n so the return value would be smaller than `len` only when EOF is reached.","attrs":[]}
{"key":"moonbitlang/async/io.PipeRead.read_some:Method","pkg":"moonbitlang/async/io","name":"read_some","parent":"moonbitlang/async/io.PipeRead","kind":"method","sig_":"pub async fn PipeRead::read_some(Self, max_len? : Int) -> Bytes?","doc":"`reader.read_some(max_len?)` fetch and return a chunk of data from the reader.\n It will return as fast as possible when new data become available.\n If EOF is reached, `None` is returned.\n\n If `max_len` is specified, the returned chunk will not be larger than `max_len`.\n Since `read_some` will return immediately when new data become available,\n the returned chunk may be smaller than `max_len`,\n even if there are still data available in the reader.","attrs":[]}
