{"key":"moonbitlang/async/js_async.ReadableStream.read_some:Method","pkg":"moonbitlang/async/js_async","name":"read_some","parent":"moonbitlang/async/js_async.ReadableStream","kind":"method","sig_":"pub async fn ReadableStream::read_some(Self, max_len? : Int) -> Bytes?","doc":"`reader.read_some(max_len?)` fetch and return a chunk of data from the reader.\n It will return as fast as possible when new data become available.\n If EOF is reached, `None` is returned.\n\n If `max_len` is specified, the returned chunk will not be larger than `max_len`.\n Since `read_some` will return immediately when new data become available,\n the returned chunk may be smaller than `max_len`,\n even if there are still data available in the reader.","attrs":[]}
{"key":"moonbitlang/async/io.PipeClosed","pkg":"moonbitlang/async/io","name":"PipeClosed","parent":"moonbitlang/async/io","kind":"type","sig_":"suberror PipeClosed","doc":"This error will be raised when\n writing to a pipe whose read end is already closed.","attrs":[]}
